### 1. Create a New Interview Session (Status: INITIALIZED)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "candidateId": "john-doe-42",
  "roleTitle": "Senior Java Developer",
  "track": "JAVA_SPRING_BOOT",
  "difficulty": "SENIOR",
  "targetCompany": "Amazon",
  "jobDescription": "Java 21, Spring Boot 3, Microservices, Concurrency"
}

### 2. Start the Session (Transitions to IN_PROGRESS)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions/1/start

### 3. Record Interviewer Question in Session Timeline
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions/1/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderRole": "AI",
  "messageType": "QUESTION",
  "content": "Can you explain how Java 21 Virtual Threads differ from OS Platform Threads?",
  "codeSnippet": null
}

### 4. Record Candidate Code Submission in Session Timeline
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions/1/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderRole": "CANDIDATE",
  "messageType": "CODE_SUBMISSION",
  "content": "Here is my virtual thread executor demonstration.",
  "codeSnippet": "try (var executor = Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()) { executor.submit(() -> System.out.println(Thread.currentThread())); }"
}

### 5. Fetch Complete Session Details & Status
GET http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions/1

### 6. Fetch Chronological Transcript
GET http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions/1/transcript

### 7. End / Complete the Session (Calculates Duration)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions/1/complete

### 8. Fetch Past Sessions for Candidate
GET http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions/candidate/john-doe-42

### 9. View In-Memory H2 Database Console
# Open http://localhost:8081/h2-console in browser (JDBC URL: jdbc:h2:mem:sessiondb, User: sa, Password: blank)


POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/sessions/1/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderRole": "CANDIDATE",
  "messageType": "CODE_SUBMISSION",
  "content": "Virtual thread executor solution",
  "codeSnippet": "var executor = Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor();"
}


